)
# The other half of "no manual pronunciation dictionary": have whichever LLM
# is already doing the translate/summarize step spell out jargon it would
# otherwise leave in the Latin alphabet, rather than relying solely on
# AUTO_DICT catching it downstream (see above). Only makes sense when the
# spoken target is actually Japanese/VOICEVOX -- TRANSLATE_TO defaults to
# that, but a deployment that repointed it elsewhere (e.g. for voiceger) gets
